<BaseLayout title="Motion Commands and Velocity Feedforward — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Motion Commands and Velocity Feedforward</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A state feedback controller and a classical P–PI cascade can be given the
    same feedback, and then they have the same poles and the same stiffness.
    What they do not share is the path a command takes in. Switch between the
    four command paths and watch the tracking of a sine change while the
    poles stay put.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
